at strangers can write, so the controls sit\n - **Budgets.** Every job has a dollar cap (`max_budget_usd`) and a hard timeout; every role and the whole repo have a daily dollar cap. The caps are enforced at the pool's claim gate (`internal/budget`): a candidate is refused when `spent >= cap`, where spent is the cost recorded in `step_usage` since 00:00 UTC today. The caps reset at 00:00 UTC and survive a restart, because spend is read from the controller database. A role's own `budget_usd_per_day` caps that role (by stage and name) alone; a role without one is limited only by the repo cap. Steps that reported no cost count as $0, and the refusal reason shows how many there were. There is no exemption for reviewers, the caps apply to OAuth credentials too, and deterministic scanners (no model, no cost) are exempt. Running jobs are never killed for a cap. If today's spend cannot be read, the gate refuses (fails closed). Each cap is logged once a day as `budget.capped`. The `budget` loop posts one comment on the status issue per capped scope (the repo, or a role) per UTC day, and records a `budget_capped` event; that event also keeps a restart from posting the notice again (a crash between comment and event can repeat one notice). The comment holds only numbers, the day and config names, no agent text and no `@`; it says the dollar figure is an estimate on a subscription and how to raise the cap (edit `budget_usd_per_day` in `.ard/config.yaml` through a reviewed PR). Under `--dry-run` the comment goes to the ledger. `--loops budget` selects the notice loop; the gate is part of the pool and is always on.\n - **Concurrency.** `max_pods` (default 3) caps every job together, and at most one triage job runs per issue at a time, because triage roles share `plan.md`; no triage job is claimed for an issue while a worker job runs on it.\n - **Kill switch.** Four sources stop new claims, scanner runs (filing and autoclose), stale closes and merges: a local pause file `~/.ard/pause/<owner>/<repo>` outside the repository (the path is lowercased; `ard serve` creates the directory, so `touch` pauses and `rm` resumes), `paused: true` in the `config.yaml` in the host's working tree, `ard:pause` on the pinned status issue, and `paused: true` in the config on `origin/main`. They are checked cheapest first, before every claiming tick. The delay is at most one loop interval plus 10% jitter; a tick already running may finish its claims. `SIGUSR1` (Unix only) makes every loop run one tick now, logged as `controller.wake`; the tick still passes the kill switch and the job pool, and wakes that arrive while a tick runs coalesce into one extra tick. The gate answers one controller-wide question and has no per-kind checks, so every loop that writes (scanner filing and autoclose, stale closes, merges, claims), except the Reaper, the cost-table writer and in-flight close-outs, must report `Claims() == true` and is skipped while paused. Running jobs, in-flight close-outs, the Reaper and the `costs` loop continue: the table is bookkeeping about work already done, not new work. The check fails closed: an unreadable status issue, a failed fetch of `origin/main`, or a config that fails to load counts as paused. The pause file pauses when anything exists at the path (a file, a directory or a symlink; content is ignored), and a path that cannot be examined, for example because `pause/<owner>` is a regular file, also counts as paused. The local working-tree `config.yaml` is read only for its `paused` key; a missing, unreadable or invalid file does not pause by itself, but a readable one that says `paused: true` does. The pause file and the local `paused` are the kill switches that nothing pushed to GitHub can lift. Config and role directories otherwise come from `origin/main` at the same SHA the tick's jobs use (see Configuration). `ard serve` remembers the status issue number in `_controller.db` (`meta` key `status_issue`). At startup it reads that issue directly and adopts it if it is still open, titled `ard status`, carries the `<!-- ard:status -->` marker and has the App as author; otherwise it searches by those same tests, and creates and pins the issue if none matches. Search is eventually consistent, so the remembered number is what stops a quick restart from creating a second issue; if two still match, the lowest number wins. A cached issue that cannot be read for a reason other than not-found falls back to search rather than aborting startup. A dry-run never stores its synthetic (negative) number; a real number found by search is stored only in the separate dry-run database. A second `ard serve` on the same repo exits with an error: the leader lock is an `flock` on `~/.ard/locks/<owner>/<repo>.lock` (local filesystem only), shared by live and dry-run.\n-- **Observability.** Every claim, close-out and failure is an event in local state. A daily digest on the pinned status issue shows queue depth by label, jobs run, failures and spend. Each issue's body also carries a per-job cost table (agent, tokens by type, cost, model, outcome and a link to the job's comment, PR) with a Total row, written by the `costs` loop. A reached daily cap is a `budget_capped` event. The repository may be public, so the spend it shows is public too; the table holds no agent text or host paths.\n+- **Observability.** Every claim, close-out and failure is an event in local state. A daily digest on the pinned status issue shows queue depth by label, jobs run, failures and spend. Each issue's body also carries a per-job cost table (agent, tokens by type, cost, model, outcome and a link to the job's comment, PR) with a Total row, written by the `costs` loop. A reached daily cap is a `budget_capped` event. The repository may be public, so the spend it shows is public too; the table holds no agent text or host paths. Scanner failure streaks (#221, the early slice of the digest, #58): each scanner posts one comment on the status issue when a failure streak starts and one when it recovers. A streak starts at the first run that is a guard trip or guard error (reason: the guard rule name or `scan-error`), any other `scan_failed` run (a `timeout` counts as `scan_failed`) or a skip at `max_open`, and ends at the next `ok` run. The posted class is kept in the scanner's `meta` table (key `failure_streak`), so a restart does not repost, and it is written only after the post succeeds. Runs dropped at the global cap and `error` runs neither start nor end a streak. A comment carries the scanner name and the reason class only, never finding text, titles, fingerprints or log lines. The post goes through the effect layer, so a dry-run logs it (`scanner.streak_notice`) and stores no streak. While the status issue number is unknown nothing is posted and the streak is not recorded, so it posts once the issue exists.\n \n ## Gaps in the original sketch\n \ndiff --git a/internal/scanner/pipeline.go b/internal/scanner/pipeline.go\nindex 29bcdef..8d52afa 100644\n--- a/internal/scanner/pipeline.go\n+++ b/internal/scanner/pipeline.go\n@@ -34,6 +34,9 @@ type Pipeline struct {\n \t// Paused reports whether the controller is paused. It is re-checked after\n \t// a scan, which can outlast a pause: a paused run files and closes nothing.\n \tPaused func(ctx context.Context) bool\n+\t// StatusIssue returns the pinned status issue number, 0 when not yet known.\n+\t// Scanner failure-streak notices are posted there. nil = none posted.\n+\tStatusIssue func() int\n \t// BodyLocks, shared with the costs loop, serialises body read-modify-writes\n \t// per issue: editIssue and join hold the issue from their fetch until the\n \t// body write is done. nil is a no-op.\n@@ -174,6 +177,7 @@ func (p *Pipeline) Run(ctx context.Context, cfg *config.Resolved, role config.Ro\n \t\tif rerr != nil {\n \t\t\tlog.Error(\"scanner.record_run_failed\", \"error\", rerr)\n \t\t}\n+\t\tp.noteRun(ctx, store, role, res)\n \t\tlog.Info(\"scanner.run\", \"sha\", res.SHA, \"outcome\", outcome, \"found\", res.Found, \"new\", res.New,\n \t\t\t\"regressions\", res.Regress, \"suppressed\", res.Suppressed, \"joined\", res.Joined, \"created\", res.Created,\n \t\t\t\"closed\", res.Closed, \"edited\", res.Edited, \"deferred\", res.Deferred, \"over_budget\", res.OverBudget,\ndiff --git a/internal/scanner/pipeline_streak_test.go b/internal/scanner/pipeline_streak_test.go\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..fc743a4\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/internal/scanner/pipeline_streak_test.go\n@@ -0,0 +1,245 @@\n+package scanner\n+\n+import (\n+\t\"context\"\n+\t\"errors\"\n+\t\"strings\"\n+\t\"testing\"\n+\n+\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/effects\"\n+\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/github\"\n+\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/state/scannerdb\"\n+)\n+\n+const streakMarker = \"PLANTED-SECRET-MARKER-123\"\n+\n+// withStatus creates a status issue in the fake and wires the pipeline to it.\n+func withStatus(t *testing.T, h *harness) int {\n+\tt.Helper()\n+\tis, err := h.gh.CreateIssue(h.ctx, github.NewIssue{Title: \"status\"})\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\th.p.StatusIssue = func() int { return is.Number }\n+\treturn is.Number\n+}\n+\n+func comments(t *testing.T, h *harness, n int) []string {\n+\tt.Helper()\n+\tcs, err := h.gh.ListComments(h.ctx, n, h.clock.AddDate(-1, 0, 0))\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\tvar out []string\n+\tfor _, c := range cs {\n+\t\tout = append(out, c.Body)\n+\t}\n+\treturn out\n+}\n+\n+type streakCase struct {\n+\tname  string\n+\tfail  func(h *harness)\n+\theal  func(h *harness)\n+\tclass string\n+}\n+\n+func streakCases() []streakCase {\n+\treturn []streakCase{\n+\t\t{\"scan_failed\", func(h *harness) { h.eng.failNext(&ScanError{SHA: \"s\", Exit: 1}) }, func(h *harness) {}, \"scan_failed\"},\n+\t\t{\"timeout\", func(h *harness) { h.eng.failNext(&ScanError{SHA: \"s\", TimedOut: true}) }, func(h *harness) {}, \"scan_failed\"},\n+\t\t{\"max_open\", func(h *harness) {\n+\t\t\th.role.MaxOpen = 1\n+\t\t\th.eng.set(fnd(\"a\", SevHigh))\n+\t\t}, func(h *harness) { h.role.MaxOpen = 5 }, \"max_open\"},\n+\t\t{\"guard\", func(h *harness) { h.eng.set(plant(fnd(\"p\", SevHigh), \"title\", planted())) },\n+\t\t\tfunc(h *harness) { h.eng.set() }, \"\"},\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+func TestStreakPostsOncePerStreak(t *testing.T) {\n+\tfor _, c := range streakCases() {\n+\t\tt.Run(c.name, func(t *testing.T) {\n+\t\t\th := newHarness(t, nil)\n+\t\t\tn := withStatus(t, h)\n+\t\t\tif c.name == \"max_open\" {\n+\t\t\t\th.eng.set(fnd(\"a\", SevHigh))\n+\t\t\t\th.mustRun() // files one issue\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t\tfor i := 0; i < 3; i++ {\n+\t\t\t\tc.fail(h)\n+\t\t\t\th.mustRun()\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t\tgot := comments(t, h, n)\n+\t\t\tif len(got) != 1 || !strings.Contains(got[0], \"`cve`\") || !strings.Contains(got[0], \"failing\") {\n+\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"after streak: %q\", got)\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t\tif c.class != \"\" && !strings.Contains(got[0], \"`\"+c.class+\"`\") {\n+\t\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"class missing: %q\", got[0])\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t\tc.heal(h)\n+\t\t\tif res := h.mustRun(); res.Outcome != OutcomeOK {\n+\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"heal run = %+v\", res)\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t\tgot = comments(t, h, n)\n+\t\t\tif len(got) != 2 || !strings.Contains(got[1], \"recovered\") {\n+\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"after recovery: %q\", got)\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t\th.mustRun()\n+\t\t\tif got = comments(t, h, n); len(got) != 2 {\n+\t\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"repost after recovery: %q\", got)\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t})\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+func TestStreakSurvivesRestart(t *testing.T) {\n+\th := newHarness(t, nil)\n+\tn := withStatus(t, h)\n+\th.eng.failNext(&ScanError{Exit: 1})\n+\th.mustRun()\n+\told := h.p\n+\tnp := *old // a restarted controller: new Pipeline, same on-disk store\n+\th.p = &np\n+\th.eng.failNext(&ScanError{Exit: 1})\n+\th.mustRun()\n+\tif got := comments(t, h, n); len(got) != 1 {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"restart reposted: %q\", got)\n+\t}\n+\th.mustRun()\n+\tif got := comments(t, h, n); len(got) != 2 || !strings.Contains(got[1], \"recovered\") {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"recovery: %q\", got)\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+func TestStreakNeutralOutcomes(t *testing.T) {\n+\th := newHarness(t, nil)\n+\tn := withStatus(t, h)\n+\th.eng.failNext(&ScanError{Exit: 1})\n+\th.mustRun()\n+\th.cfg.GlobalMaxOpen = 0\n+\tif res := h.mustRun(); res.Outcome != OutcomeGlobalCap {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"res = %+v\", res)\n+\t}\n+\th.cfg.GlobalMaxOpen = 30\n+\th.eng.failNext(errors.New(\"boom\"))\n+\tif res, _ := h.run(); res.Outcome != OutcomeError {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"res = %+v\", res)\n+\t}\n+\tif got := comments(t, h, n); len(got) != 1 {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"neutral runs changed the streak: %q\", got)\n+\t}\n+\th.eng.failNext(&ScanError{Exit: 1})\n+\th.mustRun()\n+\tif got := comments(t, h, n); len(got) != 1 {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"reposted: %q\", got)\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+func TestStreakNoFindingText(t *testing.T) {\n+\th := newHarness(t, nil)\n+\tn := withStatus(t, h)\n+\tf := fnd(\"p\", SevHigh)\n+\tf.Title += \" \" + streakMarker\n+\tf.Body = streakMarker\n+\tf.Fingerprint += \"-\" + streakMarker\n+\th.eng.set(plant(f, \"title\", planted()))\n+\th.mustRun() // guard hit\n+\th.eng.set()\n+\th.eng.failNext(&ScanError{Exit: 1, Err: errors.New(streakMarker)})\n+\th.mustRun()\n+\th.mustRun() // recovery\n+\tgot := comments(t, h, n)\n+\tif len(got) != 2 {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"comments = %q\", got)\n+\t}\n+\tfor _, b := range got {\n+\t\tif strings.Contains(b, streakMarker) || strings.Contains(b, planted()) || strings.Contains(b, \"title p\") {\n+\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"finding text in post: %q\", b)\n+\t\t}\n+\t\tif !strings.Contains(b, \"`cve`\") {\n+\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"scanner name missing: %q\", b)\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+func TestStreakDryRun(t *testing.T) {\n+\th := newHarness(t, nil)\n+\tdry, _ := effects.NewDryRun(effects.DryRunOptions{Log: quiet})\n+\th.p.Effects = dry\n+\th.p.StatusIssue = func() int { return -1 }\n+\tbuf := capture(h)\n+\th.eng.failNext(&ScanError{Exit: 1})\n+\th.mustRun()\n+\tif !strings.Contains(buf.String(), \"scanner.streak_notice\") {\n+\t\tt.Errorf(\"notice not logged: %s\", buf)\n+\t}\n+\tif v, err := h.db.Meta(h.ctx, streakKey); err == nil && v != \"\" {\n+\t\tt.Errorf(\"state written in dry-run: %q\", v)\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+func TestStreakNoStatusIssue(t *testing.T) {\n+\th := newHarness(t, nil)\n+\th.eng.failNext(&ScanError{Exit: 1})\n+\th.mustRun() // StatusIssue nil\n+\tn := 0\n+\th.p.StatusIssue = func() int { return n }\n+\th.eng.failNext(&ScanError{Exit: 1})\n+\th.mustRun() // still unknown\n+\tif v, err := h.db.Meta(h.ctx, streakKey); err == nil && v != \"\" {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"state touched: %q\", v)\n+\t}\n+\tn = withStatus(t, h)\n+\th.p.StatusIssue = func() int { return n }\n+\th.eng.failNext(&ScanError{Exit: 1})\n+\th.mustRun()\n+\tif got := comments(t, h, n); len(got) != 1 {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"comments = %q\", got)\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+type failingComments struct {\n+\tEffects\n+\tfail bool\n+}\n+\n+func (f *failingComments) CreateComment(ctx context.Context, n int, body string) (github.Comment, error) {\n+\tif f.fail {\n+\t\treturn github.Comment{}, errors.New(\"github down\")\n+\t}\n+\treturn f.Effects.CreateComment(ctx, n, body)\n+}\n+\n+func TestStreakPostFailure(t *testing.T) {\n+\th := newHarness(t, nil)\n+\tn := withStatus(t, h)\n+\tfc := &failingComments{Effects: h.fx, fail: true}\n+\th.p.Effects = fc\n+\th.eng.failNext(&ScanError{Exit: 1})\n+\tres, err := h.run()\n+\tif err != nil || res.Outcome != OutcomeScanFailed {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"res = %+v, err = %v\", res, err)\n+\t}\n+\tif v, err := h.db.Meta(h.ctx, streakKey); err == nil && v != \"\" {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"state set after failed post: %q\", v)\n+\t}\n+\tfc.fail = false\n+\th.eng.failNext(&ScanError{Exit: 1})\n+\th.mustRun()\n+\tif got := comments(t, h, n); len(got) != 1 {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"retry: %q\", got)\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+func TestStreakOldStateLoads(t *testing.T) {\n+\th := newHarness(t, nil)\n+\tif _, err := h.db.Meta(h.ctx, streakKey); !errors.Is(err, scannerdb.ErrNotFound) {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"err = %v\", err)\n+\t}\n+\tn := withStatus(t, h)\n+\th.mustRun() // ok with no streak: nothing posted\n+\tif got := comments(t, h, n); len(got) != 0 {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"comments = %q\", got)\n+\t}\n+}\ndiff --git a/internal/scanner/store.go b/internal/scanner/store.go\nindex d16cc24..8d7f8b3 100644\n--- a/internal/scanner/store.go\n+++ b/internal/scanner/store.go\n@@ -20,7 +20,9 @@ type Store interface {\n \tApply(ctx context.Context, b scannerdb.Batch) error\n \tReplace(ctx context.Context, f []scannerdb.Finding, s []scannerdb.Suppression) error\n \tRecordRun(ctx context.Context, r scannerdb.Run) (int64, error)\n-\tLastRun(ctx context.Context) (scannerdb.Run, error) // scannerdb.ErrNotFound when none\n+\tLastRun(ctx context.Context) (scannerdb.Run, error)   // scannerdb.ErrNotFound when none\n+\tMeta(ctx context.Context, key string) (string, error) // scannerdb.ErrNotFound when unset\n+\tSetMeta(ctx context.Context, key, value string) error\n }\n \n // Stores opens a scanner's Store by name.\ndiff --git a/internal/scanner/streak.go b/internal/scanner/streak.go\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..03db021\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/internal/scanner/streak.go\n@@ -0,0 +1,110 @@\n+package scanner\n+\n+import (\n+\t\"context\"\n+\t\"errors\"\n+\t\"fmt\"\n+\t\"strings\"\n+\n+\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/config\"\n+\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/state/scannerdb\"\n+)\n+\n+// streakKey is the scanner meta key holding the reason class of the open\n+// failure streak that has been posted. Absent or empty = no open streak.\n+const streakKey = \"failure_streak\"\n+\n+const maxClassLen = 64\n+\n+// classOf maps a recorded run to its streak effect. failing starts or\n+// continues a streak with the given class; ok ends one; neither = neutral.\n+// The class is a rule name or a fixed word, never finding text.\n+func classOf(res RunResult) (class string, failing, ok bool) {\n+\tswitch res.Outcome {\n+\tcase OutcomeBackpressure:\n+\t\treturn \"max_open\", true, false\n+\tcase OutcomeScanFailed:\n+\t\tif res.GuardRule != \"\" {\n+\t\t\treturn sanitiseClass(res.GuardRule), true, false\n+\t\t}\n+\t\treturn \"scan_failed\", true, false\n+\tcase OutcomeTimeout:\n+\t\treturn \"scan_failed\", true, false\n+\tcase OutcomeOK:\n+\t\treturn \"\", false, true\n+\t}\n+\treturn \"\", false, false\n+}\n+\n+// sanitiseClass keeps [A-Za-z0-9._:-], at most 64 characters.\n+func sanitiseClass(s string) string {\n+\tvar b strings.Builder\n+\tfor _, r := range s {\n+\t\tif b.Len() >= maxClassLen {\n+\t\t\tbreak\n+\t\t}\n+\t\tswitch {\n+\t\tcase r >= 'a' && r <= 'z', r >= 'A' && r <= 'Z', r >= '0' && r <= '9', r == '.', r == '_', r == ':', r == '-':\n+\t\t\tb.WriteRune(r)\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\tif b.Len() == 0 {\n+\t\treturn \"scan_failed\"\n+\t}\n+\treturn b.String()\n+}\n+\n+func streakNotice(scanner, class string) string {\n+\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"Scanner `%s` is failing: `%s`. Its runs are not completing normally; see the controller log. One notice is posted per failure streak.\", scanner, class)\n+}\n+\n+func streakRecovery(scanner string) string {\n+\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"Scanner `%s` recovered: its last run completed normally.\", scanner)\n+}\n+\n+// noteRun posts one notice when a scanner's failure streak starts and one when\n+// it ends. Errors are logged, never returned: a notice must not change the\n+// run's result.\n+func (p *Pipeline) noteRun(ctx context.Context, store Store, role config.Role, res RunResult) {\n+\tlog := p.Log\n+\tif log == nil {\n+\t\treturn\n+\t}\n+\tlog = log.With(\"scanner\", role.Name)\n+\tclass, failing, ok := classOf(res)\n+\tif !failing && !ok {\n+\t\treturn\n+\t}\n+\tctx = context.WithoutCancel(ctx)\n+\topen, err := store.Meta(ctx, streakKey)\n+\tif err != nil && !errors.Is(err, scannerdb.ErrNotFound) {\n+\t\tlog.Error(\"scanner.streak_read_failed\", \"error\", err)\n+\t\treturn\n+\t}\n+\tif failing && open != \"\" || ok && open == \"\" {\n+\t\treturn\n+\t}\n+\tvar n int\n+\tif p.StatusIssue != nil {\n+\t\tn = p.StatusIssue()\n+\t}\n+\tif n == 0 {\n+\t\tlog.Info(\"scanner.streak_unposted\", \"reason\", \"no status issue\", \"class\", class)\n+\t\treturn\n+\t}\n+\tbody, next := streakRecovery(role.Name), \"\"\n+\tif failing {\n+\t\tbody, next = streakNotice(role.Name, class), class\n+\t}\n+\tif _, err := p.Effects.CreateComment(ctx, n, body); err != nil {\n+\t\tlog.Error(\"scanner.streak_post_failed\", \"error\", err)\n+\t\treturn\n+\t}\n+\tif p.Effects.DryRun() {\n+\t\tlog.Info(\"scanner.streak_notice\", \"class\", class, \"recovered\", ok)\n+\t\treturn // a dry run never claims a streak it did not post\n+\t}\n+\tif err := store.SetMeta(ctx, streakKey, next); err != nil {\n+\t\tlog.Error(\"scanner.streak_state_failed\", \"error\", err)\n+\t}\n+}\ndiff --git a/internal/scanner/streak_test.go b/internal/scanner/streak_test.go\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..9d481ea\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/internal/scanner/streak_test.go\n@@ -0,0 +1,46 @@\n+package scanner\n+\n+import (\n+\t\"strings\"\n+\t\"testing\"\n+)\n+\n+func TestClassOf(t *testing.T) {\n+\tcases := []struct {\n+\t\tname    string\n+\t\tres     RunResult\n+\t\tclass   string\n+\t\tfailing bool\n+\t\tok      bool\n+\t}{\n+\t\t{\"backpressure\", RunResult{Outcome: OutcomeBackpressure}, \"max_open\", true, false},\n+\t\t{\"guard rule\", RunResult{Outcome: OutcomeScanFailed, GuardRule: \"aws-access-token\"}, \"aws-access-token\", true, false},\n+\t\t{\"guard error\", RunResult{Outcome: OutcomeScanFailed, GuardRule: \"scan-error\"}, \"scan-error\", true, false},\n+\t\t{\"plain scan_failed\", RunResult{Outcome: OutcomeScanFailed}, \"scan_failed\", true, false},\n+\t\t{\"timeout\", RunResult{Outcome: OutcomeTimeout}, \"scan_failed\", true, false},\n+\t\t{\"ok\", RunResult{Outcome: OutcomeOK}, \"\", false, true},\n+\t\t{\"global cap\", RunResult{Outcome: OutcomeGlobalCap}, \"\", false, false},\n+\t\t{\"error\", RunResult{Outcome: OutcomeError}, \"\", false, false},\n+\t\t{\"no slot\", RunResult{Outcome: OutcomeNoSlot}, \"\", false, false},\n+\t\t{\"paused\", RunResult{Outcome: OutcomePaused}, \"\", false, false},\n+\t\t{\"skipped\", RunResult{Outcome: OutcomeSkipped}, \"\", false, false},\n+\t}\n+\tfor _, c := range cases {\n+\t\tt.Run(c.name, func(t *testing.T) {\n+\t\t\tclass, failing, ok := classOf(c.res)\n+\t\t\tif class != c.class || failing != c.failing || ok != c.ok {\n+\t\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"got %q %v %v\", class, failing, ok)\n+\t\t\t}\n+\t\t})\n+\t}\n+}\n+\n+func TestStreakSanitise(t *testing.T) {\n+\tgot := sanitiseClass(\"bad\\nrule<!-- x -->@user\" + strings.Repeat(\"a\", 100))\n+\tif strings.ContainsAny(got, \"\\n<>@ !\") || len(got) > maxClassLen {\n+\t\tt.Errorf(\"class = %q\", got)\n+\t}\n+\tif sanitiseClass(\"\\n@\") != \"scan_failed\" {\n+\t\tt.Error(\"empty class not defaulted\")\n+\t}\n+}\ndiff --git a/internal/servecmd/scanners.go b/internal/servecmd/scanners.go\nindex c21747a..60f37ea 100644\n--- a/internal/servecmd/scanners.go\n+++ b/internal/servecmd/scanners.go\n@@ -29,6 +29,7 @@ func scannerLoop(w *wiring) controller.Loop {\n \treturn scanner.NewLoop(&scanner.Pipeline{\n \t\tReader: w.Reader, Effects: w.Effects, Committer: lc, Engine: eng,\n \t\tStores: scanner.RegistryStores(w.Scanners), Repo: w.Repo.String(), Log: w.Log, Paused: w.Paused, BodyLocks: &w.bodyLocks,\n+\t\tStatusIssue: func() int { return int(w.statusIssue.Load()) },\n \t})\n }\n \n","numLines":498,"startLine":1,"totalLines":498}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01APnhirYH72PeSXUHcLUmEH","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
